# 🔎 Database Understanding & Schema Analysis

When I receive a new dataset, I first try to understand what the data contains and how it is structured. Then, I check the tables, columns, keys, and relationships between them.

---

## 📋 1. Check Tables & Columns

I check the tables, the total number of columns in each table, the data type of each column, and the column names in each table.

```sql
SELECT
    TABLE_SCHEMA,
    TABLE_NAME,
    ORDINAL_POSITION,
    COLUMN_NAME,
    DATA_TYPE,
    CHARACTER_MAXIMUM_LENGTH,
    NUMERIC_PRECISION,
    NUMERIC_SCALE,
    IS_NULLABLE,
    COUNT(*) OVER(
        PARTITION BY TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME
    ) AS TotalColumns
FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS
ORDER BY
    TABLE_SCHEMA,
    TABLE_NAME,
    ORDINAL_POSITION;
```

