## 🔗 3. Check Existing Foreign Keys

```sql
SELECT
    OBJECT_NAME(fk.parent_object_id) AS ChildTable,
    COL_NAME(
        fkc.parent_object_id,
        fkc.parent_column_id
    ) AS ChildColumn,
    OBJECT_NAME(fk.referenced_object_id) AS ParentTable,
    COL_NAME(
        fkc.referenced_object_id,
        fkc.referenced_column_id
    ) AS ParentColumn
FROM sys.foreign_keys AS fk
JOIN sys.foreign_key_columns AS fkc
    ON fk.object_id = fkc.constraint_object_id
ORDER BY ChildTable;
```

**Result is:**

| ChildTable | ChildColumn | ParentTable | ParentColumn |
|---|---|---|---|
| FailureLogs | EquipmentID | Equipments | EquipmentID |
| FailureLogs | WorkOrderID | WorkOrders | WorkOrderID |
| WorkOrder_Parts | WorkOrderID | WorkOrders | WorkOrderID |
| WorkOrder_Parts | PartID | SpareParts | PartID |
| WorkOrders | TechnicianID | Technicians | TechnicianID |
| WorkOrders | EquipmentID | Equipments | EquipmentID |

