## 🧠 Summary

After checking the database structure, I can understand:

| Area | What I learned |
|---|---|
| 📋 Tables | What entities are available in the database |
| 🏷️ Columns | What information is stored in each table |
| 🔢 Data Types | How each field is stored |
| 🔑 Primary Keys | How each record is uniquely identified |
| 🔗 Foreign Keys | How tables are connected |
| 🧩 Relationships | How tables can be joined for analysis |
| ⚠️ Nullable Fields | Which columns may contain missing values |

This initial data understanding helps me build a clear picture of the database before moving on to **data profiling, data cleaning, transformation, and analysis**.